## How to run a stage

```
/run-stage <stage_id>
```

The slash command resolves stage_id → stage_number against the live workflow, posts to `POST /api/projects/{{ project.id }}/stages/{n}/stream`, and forwards Server-Sent Events to your terminal. Output streams live; the same StageRun row the UI watches is updated. The browser will see status flips in real time.

For stages with `config_fields`, you'll be prompted interactively. For composite stages and non-LLM stages (e.g. `synthesize_odcs_from_graph`, `auto_mapping_sa`), the same slash command picks the right backend handler.

## Reviews

Read-only from the CLI in v1. Use:

```
/reviews-pending          # counts per type + a peek at the next few items
/review-show <type> [uri] # pretty-print one item
```

To **approve / edit / escalate / reject** a review item, open the browser at `{{ frontend_base_url }}/engineer/projects/{{ project.id }}` and use `MappingReviewPanel` / `DescriptionReviewPanel` / `UnmappedColumnsPanel` / `TransformationEscalationsPanel`. The transform editor in particular has 14+ kind-specific param forms and a live SQL preview — re-implementing it as a terminal UI is deferred. Bidirectional state visibility holds: the browser approval will flip the count the next time you run `/reviews-pending`.

## Dataset-level joins override (Phase 4)

If `serving_virtual_view` raises `ViewGenerationError: ... no FK path` or the inferred FROM/JOIN graph picked the wrong bridge table, override per output dataset:

```
